  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pratap Vishwambhar Bhure vs The State Of Maharashtra on 22 July, 2025 952.25aba (1) In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No. 952 Of 2025 Pratap Vishwambhar Bhure Versus The State Of Maharashtra .....",
    "facts": "The FIR is lodged on 31/03/2025 at 21:35 hours with the Wadhwana Police Station, Dist. Latur. The offences are registered under Sections 123, 223, 274, 275 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 and under Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act. 3. The role ascribed of the present applicant in the FIR is that the alleged contraband was found in his vehicle. 4. It appears that there are several orders passed in relation to this issue by the different Courts.",
    "arguments": "The Supreme Court has recently 952.25aba (2) passed an order in Special Leave to Appeal (Cri.) No.8698/2023 in the case of Eknath Bhalchandra Patil Vs. The State of Maharashtra, Pratap Vishwambhar Bhure vs The State Of Maharashtra on 22 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/140945517/ 1 where the Supreme Court in its order dated 28/07/2023 has categorically observed that the Petitioner therein shall not be arrested in connection with Crime No.354/2022, subject to condition that he shall cooperate with the investigation. The Supreme Court has also observed that the issue regarding applicability of Section 123 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita [Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code] is pending before the Supreme Court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "The Supreme Court has recently 952.25aba (2) passed an order in Special Leave to Appeal (Cri.) No.8698/2023 in the case of Eknath Bhalchandra Patil Vs. The State of Maharashtra, Pratap Vishwambhar Bhure vs The State Of Maharashtra on 22 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/140945517/ 1 where the Supreme Court in its order dated 28/07/2023 has categorically observed that the Petitioner therein shall not be arrested in connection with Crime No.354/2022, subject to condition that he shall cooperate with the investigation. The Supreme Court has also observed that the issue regarding applicability of Section 123 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita [Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code] is pending before the Supreme Court."
  },
